# --- Large / regenerable data files ---
# Raw source extracts (106MB total) - see README "Reproducing the data" section
# for exact download/regeneration steps. Not committed to keep the repo light
# and because these are third-party FOI/Contracts Finder exports, not code.
data/raw/*.csv

# Phase 1 working directories (src/data_engineering/build_raw_from_drive.py).
# _raw_staging holds the ~500MB of original per-month FOI exports and Contracts
# Finder bulk CSVs downloaded from Google Drive; raw_ground_truth_backup is a
# local safety copy of data/raw/ taken before a rebuild. Both are regenerable
# and neither belongs in git, for the same reasons as data/raw/ above.
data/_raw_staging/
data/raw_ground_truth_backup/

# Large derived outputs (regenerated by `python -m src.run_pipeline` in ~40s).
# master_procurement_panel.csv (~79MB), anomaly_scores.csv (~38MB) and
# validation_redflags.csv (~94MB) are all close to GitHub's 100MB per-file
# limit and provide no review value as raw dumps - the small summary CSVs
# below (data_quality_report, hhi_monthly*, new_supplier_rate_by_month,
# shap_top_anomalies, spend_distribution_by_period, stl_decomposition,
# stl_shock_summary) ARE committed since they're <50KB and directly support
# the report's figures/tables.
data/processed/master_procurement_panel.csv
data/processed/anomaly_scores.csv
data/processed/validation_redflags.csv

# method_comparison_scores.csv (~59MB) is a per-record raw score dump from the
# 4-detector comparison (Stage 6A) - same rationale as above. The derived
# summary/agreement CSVs (<10KB each) are committed and drive the figures/tables.
data/processed/method_comparison_scores.csv

# fact_transactions.csv (~74MB) is the Phase 7D BI-export per-record fact
# table - same rationale as the other large per-record dumps above (close to
# GitHub's 100MB limit, no review value as a raw dump, fully regenerable via
# `python -m src.analysis.bi_export`). The dimension tables (dim_supplier,
# dim_category, dim_period, dim_month - all <500KB) ARE committed since they
# provide direct review value and are what docs/bi_dashboard_guide.md walks
# through.
data/processed/bi_export/fact_transactions.csv

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

